 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Splash Page Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a splash page?\", \"a\": \"A splash page is a screen a website shows before its home page, built around one message or one question. Visitors answer it or skip it, then continue into the site. It has no navigation of its own and usually lives at the site's root address.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a splash page?\", \"a\": \"Settle the one question or message first, then build the screen, a link into the site, and a way to remember each answer. Host it at your root address. With Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, you describe the page and where its answers go, and Emergent builds both.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the main difference between a splash page and a landing page?\", \"a\": \"A landing page is where a visitor arrives from an ad, an email, or a search result, and it asks for one conversion such as a signup. A splash page sits in front of a whole site and hands visitors on once they answer or skip. Emergent builds either kind from a prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between a home page and a splash page?\", \"a\": \"A home page is the main entry to a site, with navigation to every section. A splash page comes before it and asks for one thing. Once a visitor answers, the home page takes over, and a returning visitor should go there directly.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you give me an example of a splash page?\", \"a\": \"A concert venue whose site opens on next weekend's headline show, with Buy tickets and Enter site buttons, is a splash page. So is a game studio's full-screen trailer before its home page. Design galleries tag more splash page examples by visual style.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a splash page in a graphic novel?\", \"a\": \"In a graphic novel, a splash page is one large illustration filling the whole page in place of a grid of panels. It often opens the story and sets the place and mood. Comic artists define a splash page by that single image, and the story title and credits often sit inside it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an HTML splash page?\", \"a\": \"An HTML splash page is a single static file at the root of a site. Inside are a message, a button into the site, and a few lines of JavaScript that set a cookie. A server is needed only when the page collects something, such as an email address. On paid plans, Emergent exports the page's code to your GitHub repository.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do the best splash page examples have in common?\", \"a\": \"They ask for one decision and make the way past it as visible as the main button. The headline is short, the image loads fast, and the screen appears once instead of on every visit. Design galleries collect plenty that look good but fail the second test.\"}, {\"q\": \"What types of splash pages are there?\", \"a\": \"Website splash pages come in two kinds: gates that need an answer before entry, such as an age check, and announcements a visitor can skip. On Emergent, a gate's answers are saved to a database you own. Pages that follow an action, like a thank you page after a form, are a separate family. Mobile apps show a splash screen with the app icon while they load.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should you use a splash page instead of a landing page?\", \"a\": \"Use a splash page when every visitor to the domain must see one thing first, such as an age check or a region choice. The landing page vs splash page decision turns on the traffic. A single campaign belongs on its own page, for example an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/event-landing-page'>event landing page</a> for one date.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
